# Harr host adapter: ZCode keeps the LeanCTX MCP for CodeGraph/service gateway only.
# Native ZCode tools are the primary investigation path; CTX_* entries name the
# primary tool for each shared routing rule, not necessarily a LeanCTX tool id.
CTX_READ='native Read'
CTX_SHELL='native Bash'
CTX_SEARCH='native Grep'
CTX_GLOB='native Glob'
CTX_TOOLS='mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_tools'
CTX_CALL='mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_call'
HOST_ORCHESTRATION_POLICY='- ZCode orchestration economy: keep sequential implementation in the root chat (GLM Flash); do not spawn subagents merely to move implementation context out of the root. Spawn native subagents only for genuinely independent parallel scopes. The root owns decomposition and integration; give each subagent a bounded, self-sufficient scope and avoid dependencies between active subagents. While a subagent is active, it owns that delegated scope; the root and sibling subagents must not duplicate it. Subagents never spawn/fork agents or invoke Asa themselves; the root is the sole agent router. If a subagent reaches an unresolved material architecture decision, pause that scope and return compact evidence instead of choosing locally. On that escalation, the root must not reread or re-analyze the delegated scope: it may add only already-known global/user constraints, route the compact handoff through $asa, then forward the decision/invariants back to the SAME subagent. For an unresolved material architecture decision discovered directly by the root, the root gathers missing repository/runtime/contract facts under the normal Harr Workspace/tool-routing policy before invoking $asa, but once the boundary is material the root must not invent, rank, compare, or choose architecture alternatives. Asa is the persistent architect subagent asa-architect (the model configured for Asa) routed only through the $asa skill: first contact spawns it through the Agent tool with a compact evidence packet because it does not inherit root conversation history; later follow-ups continue the SAME agent by its agent id instead of spawning a replacement. If the Agent tool or the asa-architect subagent type is unavailable, report that ZCode Asa orchestration requires it and do not answer the material decision as root. Every Asa request declares mode=architecture-decision, mode=user-dialogue, or mode=explicit-analysis. The root transparently routes requests the user addresses to Asa and faithfully relays the Asa answer instead of answering for Asa; Asa analyzes only supplied material and never broadens into repository discovery. After Asa returns the requested decision or analysis, the existing implementation owner/context continues.'
HOST_NATIVE_POLICY='ZCode native-first routing: all workspace file reads, searches, globs, and shell work use the native ZCode tools (Read/Grep/Glob/Bash and the native editor). Never call mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_read, mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_search, mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_glob, mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_shell, or mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_call; the only Harr MCP calls are mcp__lean-ctx__ctx_tools for CodeGraph and the enabled service MCPs (and named Ein executors when configured).'
